[# docs-src/repos/cx-platform-store.cxd — the storage engine's page,
   repo-cx-platform-store.html (RULED: DOCS-41, DOCS-47, DOCS-49 wave 2).
   Facts from the registries; the one example from its own corpus (the
   journal suite). #]

[repo name=cx-platform-store
  [intro
    """State that outlives the program, addressed by content.
       `cx-platform-store` is the storage engine: a document's handle is
       derived from its canonical bytes, the journal is a hash chain, the
       live and audit streams read from the same log, full-text search sits
       beside it, and the served store answers the same two calls as an
       in-memory one."""]
  [body
    """Content addressing is the model ([[store]]): `put-doc` answers a
       handle computed from the canonical form, so the same document put
       twice is one document, and a handle is a fact about bytes rather than
       a row number. The journal appends entries whose `prev-hash` names the
       entry before, so a chain that verifies is a history nobody edited
       ([[event-evolution]], [[consistency]])."""]
  [body
    """`mem://` needs no grant and is the store every example on this site
       runs against; a real URL talks to `cx store-serve`, the daemon
       described on the [[operations]] page, with the same calls. The
       substrates, the transports, encryption at rest and the management
       console are the [[store]] page's chapters; the three streams —
       journal, live, audit — are the modules below."""]
  [gives
    """Five modules: the engine, its journal, its live and audit streams, and
       full-text search — `ft` is a Ring 1 module of this repository, the
       rest are the platform group's. Each links to the reference page the
       guide projects from the module's own documentation."""]
  [try
    """Two appends to an in-memory journal, then the second entry read back:
       its `prev-hash` is the first entry's hash, its own hash covers the
       payload, and the event rides inside it unchanged."""]
  [fixture id=journal-002-chain-link]
  [status
    """The storage engine builds on the language, the wire and the session
       layer, and is built on by the identity repository and the application
       host; the front door compiles its V module from the pin."""]]
